ity to increased ambient oxygen concentration</article-title><source>Am J Respir Cell Mol Biol</source><year>2000</year><volume>278</volume><fpage>L1240</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b24-cln63_1p0077"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balibrea</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Arias-D&#x000ed;az</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acute respiratory distress syndrome in the septic surgical patient</article-title><source>World J Surg</source><year>2003</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>1275</fpage><lpage>84</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14574489</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25-cln63_1p0077"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kudoh</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyazaki</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohara</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Fukushima</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tazawa</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamada</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Activation of alveolar macrophages in acid-injured lung in rats: different effects of pentoxifylline on tumor necrosis factor-alpha and nitric oxide production</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>1621</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11505142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b26-cln63_1p0077"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>BT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Glucocorticoids and acute lung injury</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>S253</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pu